    "title": "Banbridge Chronicle, 23 May 1936, p. 5 (\"Urban Elections: Portadown's New Council\"); nominations from the Portadown Times, 8 May 1936, p. 1 (\"The Elections: Portadown Urban Contest\")",
    "publisher": "Banbridge Chronicle (via the British Newspaper Archive)",
    "kind": "news",
    "check": "every figure read from the page image"
  },
  "note": "Triennial election held on Friday 15 May 1936 (the round due in January 1935 was put back to May 1936), declared on Saturday night. The council of fifteen was elected by the whole town: the three wards of 1923-1932 no longer appear. 4,072 votes were cast of a register of 5,202 (78 per cent); eleven spoilt. Logan, Jos. Wright, Dynes, Cooke, Orr and Cassells went forward as British Legion (ex-servicemen's) nominees; Jos. Wright and Orr were retiring members. Other labels are not printed."
